  "body": "## What changed\n\nRequested in #197: the Stock setup should show the part's dimensions to aid creating stock.\n\nThe Stock page now reads, right above the stock fields:\n\n- `Models: X x Y x Z <unit>` - the models' overall size;\n- `X min .. max   Y min .. max   Z min .. max` (dim) - their extents;\n\nin the document's units, from `model::solid_world_aabb` - the very box Fit to Models wraps (its hover says so). With no models it reads \"No models yet - load one to see its size.\" The formatting lives in a small new module, `egui_app/stock_info.rs`; the shell test sits in its own `egui_app/tests/stock_size.rs` rather than growing `tests.rs`. Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#197).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: every binary green except the lib's `egui_shell_snapshot_light` (Diff 1) and `tool_editor_snapshot` (Diff 4) - software-GL diffs with the same counts on main on this machine. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::stock_info::tests::the_readout_names_the_models_size_and_extents` (mm and inches; none with no models)\n- `egui_app::tests::stock_size::the_stock_page_shows_the_models_size` (the real Stock page on the seeded 60 x 60 x 30 block)\n\nChangelog: The Stock page shows the models' size and X/Y/Z extents\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork) - feat, merges at the next cut. #198's PR stacks on this one.\n\nFixes #197\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
